---
// GitHub Pages serves /404.html for every unknown URL. It is outside the language folders,
// so it speaks all three languages and links to each homepage.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>404 · MaptIQ</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32 48x48" />
    <style>
      body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 100vh; margin: 0; padding: 1.25rem; background: #25272b; color: #fff; text-align: center; }
      h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      p { margin: 0.4rem 0; color: #d6d7da; }
      a { color: #f5c400; font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0.6rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>404</h1>
      <p>The page you are looking for does not exist or has moved.</p>
      <p>Az oldal nem található vagy átkerült máshová.</p>
      <p>Die Seite existiert nicht oder wurde verschoben.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a href="/en/">English</a> <a href="/hu/">Magyar</a> <a href="/de/">Deutsch</a></p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
